      "id": 1,
      "text": "Walpole was first granted in 1736 as 'Number 3', a frontier fort town on the Connecticut River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walpole%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name changed to Walpole in 1761, honoring Sir Robert Walpole, Britain’s first Prime Minister.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walpole%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Walpole Academy, built in 1831 by Aaron Prentiss Howland, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
